{"name":"Koala","hex":"#b9aca0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Koala","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A West African placename\nA village and commune of Saaba department, Kadiogo, Centre, Burkina Faso.\nA village and commune of Sourgoubila department, Kourwéogo, Plateau-Central, Burkina Faso.\n A former settlement and capital of Koala, Liptako, West Africa, destroyed at the end of the eponymous kingdom by Fula rebellion\n A former kingdom in Liptako, West Africa founded by the Gourmantché people\n A former kingdom in Liptako, West Africa founded by the Gourmantché people after the destruction of the first kingdom by the Fula"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Koala"}],"entries":[{"title":"Koala","blocks":[{"text":"The koala, sometimes inaccurately called the koala bear, is an arboreal herbivorous marsupial native to Australia. It is the only extant representative of the family Phascolarctidae. Its closest living relatives are the wombats. The koala is found in coastal areas of the continent's eastern and southern regions, inhabiting Queensland, New South Wales, Victoria, and South Australia. It is easily recognisable by its stout, tailless body and large head with round, fluffy ears and large, dark nose. The koala has a body length of 60–85 cm (24–33 in) and weighs 4–15 kg (8.8–33.1 lb). Its fur colour ranges from silver grey to chocolate brown. Koalas from the northern populations are typically smaller and lighter in colour than their counterparts further south. These populations are possibly separate subspecies, but not all researchers accept this."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Koala_climbing_tree.jpg/330px-Koala_climbing_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala","wikidata":"Q36101"},{"title":"Koala (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Koala\" is a song by Dutch DJ and producer Oliver Heldens. It was released as a digital download on 16 July 2014 in the Netherlands. The song was written and produced by Oliver Heldens. The song peaked at number 42 in the Netherlands, and has also charted in Belgium."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Oliver_Heldens_Koala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koala_(song)","wikidata":"Q18161745"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Koala_Range.jpg/500px-Koala_Range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Koala_Range.jpg/1280px-Koala_Range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Koala_Range.jpg/500px-Koala_Range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoala_Range.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Nimiokoala_Litokoala.JPG/330px-Nimiokoala_Litokoala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Nimiokoala_Litokoala.JPG/330px-Nimiokoala_Litokoala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reconstructions of the ancient koalas Nimiokoala (larger), and Litokoala (smaller), from the Miocene Riversleigh Fauna","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANimiokoala_Litokoala.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Koala_skeleton1.jpg/500px-Koala_skeleton1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Koala_skeleton1.jpg/500px-Koala_skeleton1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u